        "content": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I'm Richard, a high school senior currently taking IB in Bangkok, Thailand, and I'm hoping to make some contributions to mathlib. In particular, as a starting project I'd like to try work on Hurwitz's Theorem from Diophantine approximation (which I took a course on last summer at a mathcamp). It seems like a lot of things like continued fractions and their convergents are already defined. </p>\n<p>I plan to use the proof to show that at least one of three successive convergents satisfies the bound in the theorem. Is anyone currently working on this theorem, or any abandoned PRs I can have a look at? Otherwise, any tips/advice would be most welcome as I am new to Lean. Thanks in advance!</p>",
        "id": 614069182,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuanxia Xu",
        "timestamp": 1785588494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone, I think I'm at a point where I can start work on the theorem and have come up with an elementary proof outline that avoids continued fractions. I've done a little work on some helper lemmas, could anyone look over a few examples and confirm if I'm writing these in the best way for mathlib? Thanks.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ξ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq_sqrt_five</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sq_sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">two_lt_sqrt_five</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><sp